= Systems biology — Simple =

Systems biology studies how interacting biological parts produce system-level behavior. It combines experiments with models of networks, feedback, dynamics, and multiple biological scales.

'''Important boundary:''' systems biology ≠ network diagram.

== Sources ==
* NIH/NIGMS systems-biology program definition: integration of experimental and computational approaches to biological interactions and dynamics.
* Hiroaki Kitano, “Systems Biology: A Brief Overview”, ''Science'' 295 (2002).
